THROW HTTPERROR(status, message, details) that escapes a handler responds
with its status and {"error": message, "details": details} (Requirement 6.4).
Not pinned by the spec, so not tested: whether "details" appears when
HTTPERROR is given no details.

### thrown in the handler
GET /ghosts/13
=> 404

{"error": "GHOST IS DEAD", "details": {"id": "13"}}

### thrown in a SUB the handler calls
POST /ghosts

{"age": 300}
=> 422

{"error": "A GHOST NEEDS A NAME", "details": {"missing": ["name"], "got": {"age": 300}}}

### no throw
POST /ghosts

{"name": "Casper"}
=> 200

{"created": true}
